# Java conventions

- Target **Java 21 (LTS)**; prefer modern APIs (records, sealed types, pattern matching, virtual threads) over legacy equivalents when clear. Do not use language or API features newer than 21.
- Prefer immutability for value objects; avoid public mutable fields.
- Use clear package-by-layer boundaries; do not put business logic in controllers.
- Fail fast on invalid input at API boundaries with consistent error responses.
- No secrets in source; use env / config.
